NOTICE — clean-room methodology contested (current `master` only)

The implementation on the current `master` branch was derived from a trace
document whose authoring methodology has been challenged as not satisfying
clean-room separation. The complaint, the project owner's response, and the
remediation plan are recorded in issue #3:

    https://github.com/OxideAV/oxideav-magicyuv/issues/3

References:

  * The contested trace document was deleted from the docs repo at
    OxideAV/docs commit 937a346:
      https://github.com/OxideAV/docs/commit/937a346
  * A new clean-room workspace (Specifier / Extractor / Auditor /
    Implementer roles, with explicit allow-list and forbidden-input list
    per role; FFmpeg source excluded under any path) is in place at:
      https://github.com/OxideAV/docs/tree/master/video/magicyuv
  * The forbidden-input list also covers oxideav-core commit 9a23e86, whose
    message used FFmpeg-internal identifier names ("AV_PIX_FMT_GBRP*LE
    family") in the commit text:
      https://github.com/OxideAV/oxideav-core/commit/9a23e86

Plan: once the clean-room rounds complete and a fresh implementation derived
solely from the new spec is ready, the current `master` branch will be
renamed to `old/master` for archival and a freshly-orphaned `master` will
ship the replacement implementation. The MIT licence below applies cleanly
to that replacement; for any artifact in the current branch, the
contestation status should be assessed against the issue #3 thread.

